I have the main code and understand the method to test. The key method is private static GetOverridableOption<TOptions> which calls GetKeyedService<TOptions>(key) and if null calls GetRequiredService<IOptions<TOptions>>(). I want to test that fallback call.

Since GetKeyedService<TOptions> is an extension method and not found in the immediate folders, I will test the public method GetProviderClusterOptions which calls GetOverridableOption<ClusterOptions>. This will exercise the same code path.

I will create a test class that mocks IServiceProvider to:
- Return a ClusterOptions instance for GetKeyedService to test the first branch.
- Return null for GetKeyedService and return a mocked IOptions<ClusterOptions> for GetRequiredService to test the fallback branch.

I will submit a test file with these two tests using xUnit and Moq.

